turn `orders.status` from free text into a Postgres enum. Typos like 'shiped' and 'canceled' get in today, and the dashboard's per-status counts come out wrong. Allowed values: pending, paid, shipped, cancelled, refunded.

Stack: Node 20, TypeScript, Knex migrations in `db/migrations/`. Files I expect to touch: a new migration, `src/orders/types.ts`, `src/orders/repository.ts` and `src/dashboard/counts.ts`. Commands: `npm run build`, `npm test`, `npm run lint`. Migrations run with `npx knex migrate:latest`. Don't change the JSON shape of the public REST API, and don't touch `src/payments/`. Branch: `orders-status-enum`. Rollback is the migration's `down`, which casts the column back to text.

